- dart.dev ▸ Language ▸ Enumerations
@quiz
? output: What does this print?
```dart
enum Color { red, green, blue }

void main() {
  print(Color.blue.index);
}
```
+ 2
- 3
- blue
- 1
> Indexes start at 0, so blue is 2.
? output: What does this print?
```dart
enum Color { red, green, blue }

void main() {
  print(Color.green.name);
}
```
+ green
- Color.green
- 1
- GREEN
> name returns the declared identifier as a String.
? tf: Enhanced enums can have mutable (non-final) instance fields.
= false
> Enum instance fields must be final and constructors const.
? fill: To look up an enum value from the string "hard", call `Difficulty.values.by___('hard')`.
= Name
> byName finds the value with the given name.
? scenario: You save a user's plan to local storage. Which value should you store?
+ plan.name, read back with Plan.values.byName
- plan.index
- plan.hashCode
- plan.toString().length
> Names stay stable when values are reordered.
? mcq: What is the benefit of switching over an enum without a default case?
+ The compiler reports missing cases when new values are added
- The code runs faster
- It allows null values
- It hides warnings
> Exhaustiveness checking keeps switches up to date.
